{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 0, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a film that tells the story of the founding of facebook and the subsequent legal battles that ensued. the movie begins with mark zuckerberg, played by jesse eisenberg, as a harvard undergraduate who is trying to find his place in the world. after being dumped by his girlfriend, erica, mark creates a website called facemash, which allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive.\n\nthe site becomes a huge success, but also generates a lot of controversy and gets mark into trouble with the university. this leads to mark being approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss, who ask him to help them create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees, but soon becomes obsessed with the project and begins to work on it with his friend eduardo saverin.\n\nas the site, which is initially called \"the facebook,\" begins to gain popularity, mark and eduardo's friendship starts to deteriorate. eduardo is concerned about the direction the site is taking and feels that mark is not giving him the recognition he deserves. meanwhile, the winklevoss brothers are becoming increasingly frustrated with mark, who they feel is stealing their idea.\n\nthe movie then cuts to several years later, where mark is being sued by the winklevoss brothers and eduardo. the film's narrative is presented through a series of flashbacks, as mark's lawyers try to piece together what really happened during the early days of facebook.\n\nthe social network is a well-crafted film that features strong performances from its cast. jesse eisenberg is particularly impressive as mark zuckerberg, bringing a sense of vulnerability and intensity to the role. andrew garfield is also great as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake is surprisingly good as sean parker, the co-founder of napster who becomes a key player in facebook's success.\n\nthe film's script, written by aaron sorkin, is also noteworthy. sorkin's dialogue is witty and engaging, and he does a great job of capturing the complexities of the characters and their relationships. the film's direction, courtesy of david fincher, is also impressive, with a dark and moody tone that adds to the sense of tension and unease.\n\noverall, the social network is a compelling and thought-provoking film that explores the consequences of ambition and the power of social media. it's a movie that will resonate with anyone who has ever used facebook or any other social networking site, and it's a must-see for anyone interested in the story behind one of the most popular websites in the world.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.0028338772244751453}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -0.0297507643699646}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.004086359404027462}, {"token": " a", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.35463178157806396}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.0001971527235582471}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.6843717098236084}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.005940163973718882}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -0.01826760545372963}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " facebook", "logprob": -0.00022575691400561482}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.4740769863128662}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " subsequent", "logprob": -0.5849019885063171}, {"token": " legal", "logprob": -0.953113317489624}, {"token": " battles", "logprob": -0.0015073377871885896}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.00023576818057335913}, {"token": " ensued", "logprob": -0.3166216015815735}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -1.6331539882230572e-05}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.0019384894985705614}, {"t